        "papers": 40,
        "answer": "Linear attention, state-space models, and softmax attention can be unified as special cases of a test-time regression framework defined by regression weights, function classes, and optimization algorithms (arXiv:2501.12352). A fundamental trade-off exists in long-sequence models where no architecture can simultaneously achieve per-step computation independent of sequence length, fixed-size state, and recall capacity proportional to sequence length (arXiv:2605.05066).",
